      "theme_name": "Universal Professionalization and the Decoupling of Livelihood",
      "overview": "To break the 'waged-labor' link, Benanav proposes 'Technical Associations'—modernized guilds responsible for training, accreditation, and income disbursement. This model decouples an individual's livelihood (credits) from their firm's performance (points). Firms 'rent' labor from associations at a points-denominated price that signals scarcity, while the Demos sets credit-denominated salaries based on social value. This empowers workers to act as 'multi-criterial agents' who can prioritize quality or sustainability and 'quit' unethical firms without losing income security or social status.",
