          "source_work_title": "Beyond Capitalism—2",
          "source_locator": "Section 2",
          "quote": "What must be severed is not the use of markets, but the tie between market participation and profit-seeking."
        },
        {
          "source_work_title": "Beyond Capitalism—2",
          "source_locator": "Section 2",
          "quote": "This separation ensures, first, that incomes for consumption remain limited to that. Individuals cannot use their credits to acquire productive assets, fund investments or influence collective decisions."
