    },
    {
      "theme_name": "Economy in Kind via the Non-Convertible Dual-Currency Ledger",
      "overview": "To operationalize an economy in kind while retaining decentralized flexibility, Benanav proposes a 'digital dual-currency system.' This system separates 'credits' (personal consumption) from 'points' (inter-firm transactions and investment). By making these currencies non-convertible, he de-commodifies the means of production while retaining the informational benefits of market exchange. This creates a 'Data Matrix'—a statistical mirror of the economy that tracks resources in kind. This structural break prevents market participation from translating into private profit or political power, ensuring that material constraints (labor, resources), not financial limits, govern activity.",
